<article class="env-theorem" id="4A4E3B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4A4E3B">Theorem <span data-tag="4A4E3B">2.2.1.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\calC $ a simplicial category, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a simplicial functor. The straightening and unstraightening functors determine a Quillen adjunction </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { (\sSet )_{/S}  \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{St_{\phi }} &amp;   \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }  \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{ Un_{\phi } }}, \]
</div>
  <p> where $(\sSet )_{/S}$ is endowed with the contravariant model structure and $\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }$ with the projective model structure. If $\phi $ is an equivalence of simplicial categories, then $(St_{\phi }, Un_{\phi })$ is a Quillen equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is easy to see that $St_{\phi }$ preserves cofibrations and weak equivalences, so that the pair $( St_{\phi }, Un_{\phi })$ is a Quillen adjunction. The real content of Theorem <a href="/tag/4A4E3B" data-tag="4A4E3B">2.2.1.2</a> is the final assertion. Suppose that $\phi $ is an equivalence of simplicial categories; then we wish to show that $( St_{\phi }, Un_{\phi })$ is a Quillen equivalence. We will prove this result in §<a href="/tag/817867" data-tag="817867">2.2.3</a> as a consequence of Proposition <a href="/tag/411F74" data-tag="411F74">2.2.3.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>